# {{ itsm_kb_vm_provisioning_title }}

## What the assistant should do

When a user asks to deploy a **new Apache Application stack**, launch the Ansible Automation Platform workflow job template:

**{{ aap_apache_stack_pipeline_workflow }}**

Organization: **{{ aap_apache_stack_pipeline_organization }}**

Before launching, collect every required parameter from the user (see below). Do not guess `itsm_change_ref` or `itsm_service_request_ref` — the user must supply them from the ITSM service request they submitted.

## Workflow parameters

Pass these as **extra variables** when launching **{{ aap_apache_stack_pipeline_workflow }}**:

| Parameter | Required | Meaning |
|-----------|----------|---------|
| `itsm_change_ref` | yes | ITSM standard change reference created by the service request (e.g. `CHG-6`). Used to start and complete change tasks (CTASKs) during the workflow. |
| `itsm_service_request_ref` | no | ITSM service request reference for audit (e.g. `REQ-3`). Optional but recommended when the stack was requested via the ITSM catalog. |
| `vm_name` | yes | Unique name for the new virtual machine. Also used as the Ansible target host for Apache deployment. Must match the value on the service request. |
| `cpus` | yes | Number of CPU cores for the VM (integer, e.g. `2`). |
| `mem` | yes | Memory for the VM in GiB (integer, e.g. `4`). |
| `app_repo` | yes | Gitea repository name containing the Apache application to deploy (e.g. `AIOps_App`). |
| `app_branch` | no | Git branch to deploy from `app_repo`. Default: `main`. |

## What to ask the user

The assistant must obtain from the user:

1. **`itsm_change_ref`** — from the ITSM change linked to their Apache stack service request.
2. **`itsm_service_request_ref`** (if available) — from the submitted service request.
3. **`vm_name`**, **`cpus`**, **`mem`**, **`app_repo`**, and optionally **`app_branch`** — the stack specifications (same values as on the service request).

If the user has not submitted an ITSM service request yet, direct them to catalog request **{{ itsm_apache_stack_request_template_name }}** first, then use the returned `CHG-*` and `REQ-*` references when launching the workflow.

## Example launch (extra vars)

```yaml
itsm_change_ref: CHG-6
itsm_service_request_ref: REQ-3
vm_name: server01
cpus: 2
mem: 4
app_repo: AIOps_App
app_branch: main
```

